    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pitkas Point has no road links; travelers must fly via scheduled bush planes or charter boats, and schedules shift with weather.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.traveldojo.com/pitkas-point-alaska/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pitkas Point experiences a subarctic climate, with cool summers peaking in July and freezing winters that hit their lowest in January.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.traveldojo.com/pitkas-point-alaska/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The best time to visit Pitkas Point is June through August, when milder weather, long daylight, and reliable access make travel easier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.traveldojo.com/pitkas-point-alaska/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Pitkas Point is a remote coastal settlement where visitors can spot diverse bird species, join subsistence fishing, and explore wide Arctic shorelines by charter flight or boat.",
